    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"Data compiled by two separate groups has produced sets of metallogenic data for both North America and for South America.  These data have subsequently been published in both map and text form  (North American Metallogenic Map Committee, 1981; Guild, 1981a; Guild, 1981b; Martin, C. (coordinator), 1983; Guild, 1987).  In order to concisely present this metallogenic information, both the North and South American compilations relied on specially developed map symbols and on alpha-numeric codes to present these data in text form.  Respectively the North American  and South American data sets contained information on 4,215 and 2,511 mineral deposits and occurrences.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
